 "reading": "Pleat 2 does not hide 'OH? REALLY?' cleanly: the balloon (2114-2316) is cut at 2210, so the left of 'OH? / REALLY?' and the right end of 'I HAD IT' disappear and the boys lose their left half. It yields no coherent new utterance, which is why the work uses one pleat. To hide the boys' line wholly a pleat would need A2 <= 2102 and B2 >= 2328, i.e. D2 >= 226 with both edges inside P2 (for example A2 = 2090, M2 = 2210, B2 = 2330) - but that also cuts the boys' figures.",
 "order_of_operations": "On a copy already folded with pleat 1 (A-first, then M), pleat 2 acts on the folded packet in x' coordinates: A2' = A2 - D = 810, M2' = 920. The visible faces are the same as folding pleat 2 first and then pleat 1 (they act on disjoint ranges: pleat 1 on 620-1800, pleat 2 on 1990-2210), but the light-box stack differs: pleat 2 adds two layers over x' 810-920 only."
}